course: dictionary
lesson: 8644
title: Meet the seahorse
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A seahorse is a small fish. Its head is shaped like a horse's head, its tail is curled, and it swims upright, standing up in the water instead of lying flat like most fish.
explain: Read this sentence: «Seahorses are fish that swim upright and grip seaweed with curly tails.» Upright means standing straight up, and curly tails tell you how they hold on. These context clues help you picture the word.
explain: Seahorses have a surprise too. «The male carries the eggs in a pouch until the babies hatch.» The father looks after the eggs, not the mother. Even though it is called a seahorse, remember that it is a fish.
fact: A seahorse is a small fish that swims upright.
fact: Its head is shaped like a horse's head, and its tail is curled.
fact: The father seahorse carries the eggs in a pouch until the babies are born.
fact: Seahorses live in shallow warm seas, among seagrass and coral reefs.
fact: They hold on to plants with their tails and eat tiny shrimp.
exercise: «A seahorse is a fish: it has gills and fins and lives in water all its life.» What is a seahorse? | A kind of horse that lives on land | *A small fish | A bird that lives in trees | A plant on the sea floor
exercise: «Seahorses are fish that swim upright and grip seaweed with curly tails.» What do seahorses use their tails for? | To sing to other fish | To swim very fast | To carry eggs | *To hold on to plants
exercise: «Seahorses are fish that swim upright and grip seaweed with curly tails.» Find and copy one word that means standing straight up. | seaweed | curly | pouch | *upright
test: The seahorse's head is shaped like what? | A bird's head | *A horse's head | A frog's head | A dog's head
test: «The male carries the eggs in a pouch until the babies hatch.» Who carries the eggs? | *The father | The shrimp | The mother | The babies
exam: Why does a seahorse curl its tail round seaweed? | To rest and keep warm | To hide its eggs | To swim faster | *To hold on
